# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RoboApply — environment variables
#
# Local dev: copy to `.env` (loaded by server/src/app.ts + prisma) and put the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars in `.env.local` for Next.js. On Vercel, set these in
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables (never commit real secrets).
#
# This file is the catalogue: every name the API (server/src) or the web app
# reads is listed here once with its purpose (audited in INT-13). Names only,
# never a real value. Both brands run from this one file (owner ruling D5):
# NAME is the shared value RoboApply uses, and CN_NAME is an OPTIONAL override
# for GoApply. With no CN_ value at all GoApply works on the shared stack (the
# rule, by class of name, is under "Jobright clone" below). The mainland
# stack's subset is deploy/cn/cn.env.example (API pods) and
# deploy/cn/cn.web.env.example (web pods).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development
# Express API port for local dev (the Next app runs on 3611).
PORT=4607
# Proxy hops Express trusts when it reads X-Forwarded-For into req.ip (the
# rate-limit key): true | false | a hop count | an Express subnet list. Unset:
# true on Vercel (unchanged), 1 on every other host (the mainland gateway and
# `next dev` are one proxy). See roboapply/schedulers/processLifecycle.ts.
# TRUST_PROXY=1
# How long SIGTERM / SIGINT waits for running requests before the process
# exits, in ms (listening hosts only). Unset: 305000 in production, 1000 in dev.
# SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Logging: DEBUG | INFO | WARN | ERROR; log files go to LOG_DIR (default ./logs)
# unless FILE_LOGGING=false (always off on Vercel, whose filesystem is read-only).
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# LOG_DIR=
# FILE_LOGGING=true

# ── Database (shared Neon with RoboHire for now) ────────────────────────────
# Runtime uses the POOLED (pgbouncer) Neon endpoint. For serverless, append
# ?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1 to the pooled URL.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DB?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1
# DIRECT (non-pooler) endpoint — used ONLY by `prisma db push` / migrations
# (DDL over the transaction pooler silently no-ops).
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DB?sslmode=require
# Keep pooled connections warm on a long-running host (default on; off on
# Vercel unless set to true), and the ping interval in ms (default 90000).
# PRISMA_KEEPALIVE_ENABLED=
# PRISMA_KEEPALIVE_MS=
# Interactive-transaction limits for every Prisma client (server/src/lib/prisma.ts).
# PRISMA_TX_MAX_WAIT_MS: how long a `$transaction` may wait for a connection
# (default 10000; Prisma's own default of 2000 is shorter than a cold pooled
# Neon connection). PRISMA_TX_TIMEOUT_MS: how long it may run (default 20000).
# Keep the wait below 30000 (the pool's connect timeout) so a busy database
# answers a retryable 503 `credits_busy` instead of a 500.
# PRISMA_TX_MAX_WAIT_MS=
# PRISMA_TX_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Connections per pool (default 10 on a long-running host, 1 on Vercel). An
# interactive transaction holds one connection for its whole length, so with 1
# it blocks every other query in that instance; consider 3-5 on Vercel.
# PRISMA_POOL_MAX=

# ── Auth / cookies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
SESSION_EXPIRES_IN=30d
# For same-site cookies across roboapply.io and its api. Leave unset in dev.
# COOKIE_DOMAIN=.roboapply.io
# SameSite of the session cookie: lax (default) | strict | none.
# COOKIE_SAME_SITE=lax
# Email verification at signup: false turns it off; link lifetime in hours (default 24).
# EMAIL_VERIFICATION_ENABLED=true
# EMAIL_VERIFICATION_TTL_HOURS=24
# AES-256-GCM key for field secrets stored in the database, such as a user's
# own LLM key (lib/crypto.ts): 64 hex chars (openssl rand -hex 32), or a
# passphrase the key is derived from. Unset → encrypting or reading one throws.
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# Business-email gate inherited from the recruiter product (lib/emailDomainPolicy.ts):
# false turns it off; comma lists force-allow / force-block domains.
# BUSINESS_EMAIL_ONLY=
# BUSINESS_EMAIL_ALLOWLIST=
# BUSINESS_EMAIL_BLOCKLIST=
# Days a closed account is kept before the nightly purge deletes it (default 30).
# ACCOUNT_PURGE_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# ── Public URLs (Next.js — put these in .env.local for dev) ─────────────────
# In PRODUCTION keep NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL EMPTY so the browser calls same-origin
# /api/v1/* (Vercel rewrites route them to the Express function). In dev, the
# Next rewrite proxies /api/* to this backend at NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4607
NEXT_PUBLIC_ROBOAPPLY_URL=http://localhost:3611
# Origin of the RoboHire recruiter site, for links that send a recruiter out
# of this app (lib/config.ts). Unset → derived from an api.* NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
# else http://localhost:3607.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ROBOHIRE_URL=
# Dev/browser checks only: true shows nav entries that are not flagged ready yet.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_ALL_NAV=
# Dev only: true serves the frozen V2 client from in-browser fixtures (lib/stub).
# Never set it in a deployed build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_STUB_API=
# Used by outbound emails / OAuth redirects / public links in production.
APP_URL=https://roboapply.io
PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://roboapply.io
# Older aliases still read as fallbacks: FRONTEND_URL (email links, after
# APP_URL / PUBLIC_APP_URL) and ROBOAPPLY_URL (the app origin billing links
# use, after NEXT_PUBLIC_ROBOAPPLY_URL). Prefer the names above.
# FRONTEND_URL=
# ROBOAPPLY_URL=
# Extra browser origins allowed by CORS, comma list (besides the brand hosts).
# FRONTEND_URLS=
# Preview deployments that may call the API with credentials: comma list of
# host globs (`*` = letters, digits and hyphens inside one label), e.g. this
# project's own Vercel preview hosts. Unset, blank, `none` or `off` = no
# preview origin is allowed. A bare `*.vercel.app` is refused.
# Careful with any pattern under vercel.app: another Vercel account can claim
# a project name that matches it, so list this project's exact preview hosts.
# CORS_PREVIEW_HOSTS=

# ── Vercel Cron ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel sends `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` to /api/v1/cron/* routes.
CRON_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# The in-process node-cron is auto-disabled on Vercel (VERCEL is set). Set this
# to true to disable it on any other always-on host too.
# ROBOAPPLY_CRON_DISABLED=false
# node-cron mirror only: time zone of the schedules (default UTC) and the two
# legacy schedules (defaults 0 6 * * * and 0 4 * * *).
# SCHEDULER_TZ=UTC
# ROBOAPPLY_RENEWAL_REMINDER_CRON=
# ROBOAPPLY_ACCOUNT_PURGE_CRON=

# ── LLM providers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-token costs are NOT configured here: the billed rates live in
# server/src/lib/modelCostTable.ts (rendered to docs/LLM_COSTS.md by
# `npm run llm:costs`). That command also reports which of the models selected
# below have no cost-table row and would bill at the default tier.
LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
LLM_MODEL=openrouter/google/gemini-3-flash-preview
# Task-specific model and reasoning-effort settings. Model values may use a
# direct provider prefix (deepseek/..., openai/...) or openrouter/... routing.
# Effort values: minimal|low|medium|high|max (provider support varies; the
# LiveKit interview worker supports minimal through high, not max).
LLM_MATCHING_MODEL=
LLM_MATCHING_REASONING_EFFORT=
LLM_EXTRACT_MODEL=
LLM_EXTRACT_REASONING_EFFORT=
LLM_ONBOARDING_MODEL=
LLM_ONBOARDING_REASONING_EFFORT=
LLM_REWRITE_MODEL=
LLM_REWRITE_REASONING_EFFORT=
LLM_INTERVIEW_MODEL=
LLM_INTERVIEW_REASONING_EFFORT=
# Live interviewer turns (the LiveKit worker). Unset → LLM_INTERVIEW_MODEL.
# The ALIGNED_INTERVIEW_MODELS allowlist applies to this value. When the
# effort is unset, reasoning families (openai gpt-5*/gpt-6*/gpt-oss/o-series)
# get 'low' and every other model gets none, so live turns stay fast.
LLM_INTERVIEW_LIVE_MODEL=
LLM_INTERVIEW_LIVE_REASONING_EFFORT=
# Blueprint/prompt generation during POST /sessions/:id/prepare. Unset →
# LLM_INTERVIEW_MODEL. A faster model here shortens the "Preparing" screen.
LLM_INTERVIEW_BLUEPRINT_MODEL=
LLM_INTERVIEW_BLUEPRINT_REASONING_EFFORT=
# Fallback route when the primary call fails. The admin DB override wins over
# this value. It is tried on auth/billing failures (401/402/403, "User not
# found.", invalid key, no credits) and on transient overload
# (429/503/timeout/empty output). Accepts any selector, e.g.
# google/gemini-3.8-flash or openrouter/openai/gpt-6-luna.
# When unset, an auth/billing failure still reroutes through the first DIRECT
# provider with a key (system DB key or env), in this order:
#   google/gemini-3.8-flash → anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 →
#   deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash → openai/gpt-6-luna
# The auto route never selects OpenRouter. It never applies to BYOK calls.
# A transient blip without a configured fallback stays on the primary, where
# withLLMRetry retries it. A provider whose platform key fails auth/billing is
# skipped for 10 minutes (an in-process circuit breaker); rotating the key
# closes the circuit at once.
LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# Set to false to disable the auto-selected route (LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL still applies).
# LLM_FALLBACK_AUTO=true
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Global reasoning-effort dial, applied to every model that exposes one and
# silently ignored by those that don't. minimal|low|medium|high (OpenAI direct +
# OpenRouter); DeepSeek accepts high|max; Anthropic accepts low|medium|high|max.
# Unset = each provider's own default. Task-specific efforts above win, followed
# by admin/provider tuning and provider-specific env vars.
# LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
# Optional DB-backed LLM settings kill-switch (true = pure-env behaviour).
# LLM_SETTINGS_DB_DISABLED=false
# Endpoint overrides per provider (unset = the vendor's own host). RoboApply
# prompts are refused on a mainland host. GoApply prompts may go wherever
# RoboApply's may, plus the domestic vendors; CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY=true (below)
# limits GoApply to mainland hosts.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# OPENROUTER_API_BASE_URL=
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# DEEPSEEK_API_BASE_URL=
# KIMI_API_BASE_URL=
# MINIMAX_BASE_URL=
# Self-hosted routes: an Ollama server and a `newapi` gateway (key + base URL each).
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# NEWAPI_BASE_URL=
# NEWAPI_API_KEY=
# Sent as X-Proxy-Key to an LLM reverse proxy placed in front of a vendor
# (used with that vendor's base URL override; env only).
# LLM_PROXY_KEY=
# Request timeout in ms for every provider, and per provider (wins over the global).
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# OPENAI_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# OPENROUTER_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# GOOGLE_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# ANTHROPIC_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# DEEPSEEK_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# KIMI_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Retries of a failed call (attempts, first delay and delay cap in ms), and the
# vendor SDKs' own retry count (leave unset unless you have a reason).
# LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=
# LLM_RETRY_BASE_MS=
# LLM_RETRY_MAX_MS=
# LLM_SDK_MAX_RETRIES=
# DeepSeek only: thinking mode (enabled|disabled), effort (high|max) and the
# extra tokens reserved for reasoning on a thinking call (default 8000).
# DEEPSEEK_THINKING_MODE=
# DEEPSEEK_REASONING_EFFORT=
# DEEPSEEK_REASONING_MAX_TOKENS=
# Purpose selectors inherited from the recruiter LLM stack (unset → LLM_MODEL).
# The resolver (lib/llm/llmModels.ts) reads each of them; RoboApply's own
# features are driven by the task settings above.
# LLM_FAST=
# LLM_PRO=
# LLM_VISION_MODEL=
# LLM_QUICK_JOB=
# LLM_EVALUATION=
# LLM_MATCH_RESUME=
# LLM_MATCH_SCREEN=
# LLM_PREMATCH_FILTER=
# LLM_JOB_TAG=
# LLM_RESUME_TAG=
# LLM_INTENT_PARSER=
# LLM_CRM_HEALTH=
# LLM_CRM_PROFILE=
# LLM_CRM_EMAIL=
# LLM_CRM_DIGEST=
# LLM_CRM_COACHING=
# LLM_AGENT_ALEX=
# Per-agent model overrides of the legacy V2 agents (unset → the task model):
# the weekly summary, and the resume tailor's standard and deep passes.
# RA_V2_CAREER_INSIGHT_MODEL=
# RA_V2_RESUME_TAILOR_MODEL_STANDARD=
# RA_V2_RESUME_TAILOR_MODEL_DEEP=
# Local runs without a model: true makes every LLM call return a canned
# minimal answer (an empty object for JSON callers). Never set it in production.
# MOCK_LLM=

# ── Web search (RA insights / interview grounding) ──────────────────────────
TAVILY_API_KEY=
# Billed cost per Tavily credit / Firecrawl page in USD (defaults in lib/modelPricing.ts).
# TAVILY_COST_PER_CREDIT_USD=
# FIRECRAWL_COST_PER_PAGE_USD=

# ── Stripe (RoboApply consumer billing) ─────────────────────────────────────
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Webhook: point a Stripe endpoint at /api/v1/roboapply/stripe/webhook
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Or a RoboApply-specific secret if you split the endpoint:
# ROBOAPPLY_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_ROBOAPPLY_STARTER_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_ROBOAPPLY_GROWTH_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_ROBOAPPLY_PREMIUM_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_ROBOAPPLY_PREMIUM_PLUS_PRICE_ID=
# Legacy rate-card row for the free tier (normally unset).
# STRIPE_ROBOAPPLY_FREE_PRICE_ID=
# Legacy practice plans (lib/mockInterviewPlans.ts): minutes one credit covers
# (default 20), credits per plan, and plan prices in minor units (cents / fen).
# RA_MOCK_CREDIT_MINUTES=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_FREE_CREDITS=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_STARTER_CREDITS=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_STARTER_USD_MINOR=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_STARTER_CNY_MINOR=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_GROWTH_CREDITS=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_GROWTH_USD_MINOR=
# RA_MOCK_PLAN_GROWTH_CNY_MINOR=
# Days a lapsed subscription keeps access (lib/subscriptionGraceConfig.ts).
# SUBSCRIPTION_GRACE_DAYS=
# Legacy usage gates inherited from the recruiter product: `disabled` turns the
# free-trial gate off; false turns overage billing off; true enables its
# obsolete shadow mode (a ledger row without a debit).
# FREE_TRIAL_GATING=
# OVERAGE_ENABLED=
# OVERAGE_SHADOW=

# ── Alipay (RMB market; the existing rail, D6) ──────────────────────────────
# GoApply sells its passes through this rail. Its request, callback and
# verification path must keep working exactly as it does (additive changes only).
# Payment worker endpoint. Optional: unset = the default worker
# (https://worker.gohire.top/payment/payment/create).
ALIPAY_API_URL=
# The rail's own credential, as STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is Stripe's. Required to open
# a payment and for every Alipay callback, legacy RoboApply orders included.
# Unset: GoApply still lists its plans and prices but cannot open a payment,
# callbacks answer 503 and orders stay pending (WP-21a). This value alone opens
# GoApply payments: no price variable and no CN_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true is needed.
ALIPAY_CALLBACK_SECRET=
# Optional callback origin override for RoboApply; defaults to
# https://www.roboapply.io. Must serve /api/v1/roboapply/billing/alipay/callback
# (not api.robohire.io). For local webhook testing, use the public URL of a
# tunnel to this API. Brand-own: GoApply reads CN_BACKEND_URL (below), never this.
# BACKEND_URL=https://www.roboapply.io

# ── Interview Engine (LiveKit voice/video mock interviews) ──────────────────
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
# Read into the LiveKit credentials but not used: the worker is dispatched by
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_AGENT_NAME (on GoApply's own media plane:
# CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_AGENT_NAME). Leave this and CN_LIVEKIT_AGENT_NAME unset.
# LIVEKIT_AGENT_NAME=

# ── Object storage (R2 / S3 — resume originals + Egress recordings) ─────────
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_REGION=auto
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
# AWS_* fall-backs are also read by the AWS SDK.
AWS_REGION=
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Where uploaded resume originals go: s3 | local | none. Unset: s3 when the
# bucket and keys above are set, else local in dev and none in production.
# Key prefix in the bucket (default resume-originals) and the local folder.
# RESUME_FILE_STORAGE_PROVIDER=
# RESUME_FILE_STORAGE_PREFIX=
# RESUME_FILE_STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR=
# PDF text extraction: parse and pdftotext timeouts in ms, the characters per
# page below which the text layer is rejected (default 200), and the vision-OCR fallback's
# concurrency, attempts per page, minimum share of pages that must succeed
# (0–1) and longest image edge in px.
# PDF_PARSE_TIMEOUT_MS=
# PDF_PDFTOTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS=
# PDF_MIN_CHARS_PER_PAGE=
# PDF_VISION_CONCURRENCY=
# PDF_VISION_PAGE_ATTEMPTS=
# PDF_VISION_MIN_SUCCESS_RATIO=
# PDF_VISION_MAX_EDGE_PX=

# ── Email ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared email transport (Resend). GoApply sends through it too unless
# CN_EMAIL_TRANSPORT (below) names another transport.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# RoboApply sender. ROBOAPPLY_EMAIL_FROM is read first, then EMAIL_FROM, then the
# brand default. GoApply's own sender is CN_EMAIL_FROM; without it GoApply mail
# sent through Resend uses this verified address under the display name GoApply.
ROBOAPPLY_EMAIL_FROM=RoboApply <noreply@roboapply.io>
# EMAIL_FROM=

# ── External job boards / enrichment (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# The job-search workspace queries configured live sources. The three original
# RapidAPI job-search services share ONE key, but each
# service must be separately SUBSCRIBED on your RapidAPI app:
#   • JSearch            (jsearch.p.rapidapi.com)             — global aggregator
#   • Active Jobs DB     (active-jobs-db.p.rapidapi.com)      — direct-employer ATS
#   • LinkedIn Job Search(linkedin-job-search-api.p.rapidapi.com) — LinkedIn feed
# Each provider self-guards (in-process LRU cache + circuit breaker + a
# per-process daily billed-call budget) and NEVER throws — a missing key,
# missing subscription, or open breaker degrades that provider to silent no-op.
RAPID_API_KEY=
# Global kill switch — 'true' disables ALL external job providers at once.
RA_ONBOARDING_EXTERNAL_JOBS_DISABLED=
# Per-provider kill switches — 'true' hard-offs one provider without touching
# the key (e.g. to stop billing a service while keeping the others live).
RA_ONBOARDING_JSEARCH_DISABLED=
RA_ONBOARDING_ACTIVEJOBS_DISABLED=
RA_ONBOARDING_LINKEDIN_JOBS_DISABLED=
# Per-provider per-process daily billed-call budgets (integer; default 300).
# Sized to your RapidAPI monthly plan for that service ÷ ~30.
RA_ONBOARDING_JSEARCH_DAILY_BUDGET=
RA_ONBOARDING_ACTIVEJOBS_DAILY_BUDGET=
RA_ONBOARDING_LINKEDIN_JOBS_DAILY_BUDGET=
# Posting-age window the Active Jobs DB / LinkedIn feeds query: 7d (default) | 24h.
# RA_ONBOARDING_FANTASTIC_WINDOW=
# Shared website/API search service, on both brands (D5). RoboApply searches
# the providers listed here (IDs: jsearch,activejobs,linkedin,hiringindex).
# GoApply searches its own index of mainland postings (provider id `index`);
# no RapidAPI provider is ever called for GoApply.
JOB_SEARCH_PROVIDERS=jsearch,activejobs
# External integration rights must be established independently of subscriptions.
# Empty means no provider data is returned through the partner API, on either
# brand. The id `index` grants GoApply's own index to integration keys.
JOB_SEARCH_API_PROVIDERS=
JOB_SEARCH_DISABLED=
# GoApply per-key overrides of the two settings above (the general rule:
# CN_NAME when set, else NAME).
# CN_JOB_SEARCH_API_PROVIDERS=
# CN_JOB_SEARCH_DISABLED=
JOB_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# Planning deadline; the agent uses the existing intent-parser/fast/default LLM settings.
JOB_SEARCH_AGENT_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
JOB_SEARCH_CACHE_TTL_MS=300000
# Durable search-attempt limits across replicas and all keys of each owner.
JOB_SEARCH_USER_PER_MINUTE=10
JOB_SEARCH_USER_DAILY_LIMIT=100
JOB_SEARCH_GLOBAL_DAILY_LIMIT=250
# Optional adapter, only used when explicitly allowlisted and subscribed.
JOB_SEARCH_HIRINGINDEX_DISABLED=
JOB_SEARCH_HIRINGINDEX_DAILY_BUDGET=100

# ── Interview engine (LiveKit voice worker contract) ────────────────────────
# The control plane (this .env) and the worker (interview-agent/.env.local)
# MUST agree on these two values, or dispatches go to nobody / callbacks are
# rejected (empty transcripts + all-zero reports). On the shared media plane
# this one worker, its callback secret and the callback origin below serve
# both brands' sessions.
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_AGENT_NAME=RoboApply-Interview
LIVEKIT_AGENT_CALLBACK_SECRET=   # openssl rand -hex 24; same value in interview-agent/.env.local
# Public API origin the worker posts transcripts/lifecycle callbacks to. Set it
# explicitly in production. When unset in production (VERCEL=1 or
# NODE_ENV=production), the origin of the create request is used, but only if
# its host is on the allowlist (roboapply.io, robohire.io, goapply.top, the
# Vercel project URLs, plus the comma list below). Dev default:
# http://localhost:$PORT.
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_CALLBACK_BASE_URL=
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_CALLBACK_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Older aliases of INTERVIEW_ENGINE_CALLBACK_BASE_URL, read after it (for both
# brands' sessions on the shared plane; GoApply's own plane reads the CN_ value).
# BACKEND_PUBLIC_URL=
# PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=
# Preparation limits: the web-evidence (Tavily) stage, and one whole prepare
# run. Keep the latter under the Vercel maxDuration (300 s).
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_WEB_EVIDENCE_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_PREPARE_TIMEOUT_MS=240000
# Record practice audio/video to R2. Opt-in: unset means off, so storing a
# session never starts silently once storage credentials work.
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_RECORDING_ENABLED=false
# Speech models of the RoboApply worker (LiveKit Inference ids). STT default
# deepgram/nova-3 with fallback deepgram/nova-2 (comma list; empty = none).
# TTS provider/model override every locale; per-locale voice ids and models:
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_VOICE_<LOCALE>[_MALE] and INTERVIEW_ENGINE_MODEL_<LOCALE>[_MALE]
# (locale upper-cased, e.g. EN, ZH, ZH_TW, JA, KO).
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_MODEL=
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_FALLBACK_MODELS=
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_PROVIDER=
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_MODEL=
# Join-token lifetime in seconds (default 3600) and minutes before an unfinished
# session expires (default 120).
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_JOIN_TOKEN_TTL_SEC=
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_SESSION_EXPIRY_MIN=
# Cost rates for the session cost report (USD): STT per minute (default and the
# nova-2 rate), TTS per 1M characters and per minute, recording egress per GB,
# stored artifacts per GB-month.
# INTERVIEW_STT_USD_PER_MIN=
# INTERVIEW_STT_USD_PER_MIN_NOVA2=
# INTERVIEW_TTS_USD_PER_1M_CHARS=
# INTERVIEW_TTS_USD_PER_MIN=
# RA_EGRESS_USD_PER_GB=
# RA_STORAGE_USD_PER_GB_MONTH=
# Speech vendor keys. The API never calls these vendors itself: it only checks
# whether they are set, to list Deepgram / Cartesia as sub-processors in the
# privacy disclosures; scripts/parley-provision.ts passes them to a Parley node.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# CARTESIA_API_KEY=
# Local node-cron schedule for expiring stale preparing/created/live sessions
# (Vercel runs /api/v1/cron/interview-cleanup from vercel.json instead).
ROBOAPPLY_INTERVIEW_CLEANUP_CRON=*/15 * * * *

# ── Parley pilot (practice interviews without LiveKit) ─────────────────────
# Parley is a standalone WebRTC interview service (its own VAD/STT/LLM/TTS):
# the browser connects to it directly, so a pilot session needs no LiveKit
# room, agent dispatch or interview-agent worker. Transcripts, scoring,
# reports and credits are unchanged. Off unless INTERVIEW_ENGINE_PARLEY_PILOT
# is "all" or a comma list of user emails / ids; decided once per session at
# creation, candidate practice only, for users of both brands (GoApply sessions
# stay on LiveKit under CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY or the strict posture). Needs
# LIVEKIT_AGENT_CALLBACK_SECRET above.
# `npx tsx --env-file=.env scripts/parley-provision.ts --admin-password …`
# configures a Parley node and prints the PARLEY_* lines. Parley calls
# INTERVIEW_ENGINE_CALLBACK_BASE_URL + /api/v1/interview-engine/webhooks/parley.
# Production: deploy a node with Parley's deploy/deploy.sh (runbook in its
# deploy/README.md), then scripts/parley-vercel-env.sh <output> <allowlist>.
INTERVIEW_ENGINE_PARLEY_PILOT=off
PARLEY_URL=                 # e.g. http://localhost:8080 — the browser connects here too (https in production)
PARLEY_API_KEY=             # pk_…
PARLEY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=      # whsec_…
PARLEY_AGENT_ID=            # agt_… (STT/LLM/TTS stack; prompt/opening/language are per session)
PARLEY_TTS_PROFILES=        # optional voice per language, e.g. en:tts_…,zh:tts_…
PARLEY_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=    # optional: origin Parley calls back at, e.g. http://host.docker.internal:4611 for Parley in local Docker

# ── Cross-bank job search (RoboApply candidate side) ──────────────────────
# The candidate app searches BOTH recruiter job banks at once. Each is a
# separate physical Postgres with the identical Prisma schema. Leave unset to
# fall back to the active brand's own DB (single-bank cross-DB is the safe
# default; reading the FOREIGN brand's bank additionally requires the
# cross-tenant sign-off flag below).
DATABASE_URL_ROBOHIRE=
DATABASE_URL_GOHIRE=
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL_ROBOHIRE=
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL_GOHIRE=
# Legacy recruiter-bank selectors (lib/brand.ts, lib/databaseUrl.ts). Leave
# unset here: APP_NAME / BRAND = gohire would make this API read
# DATABASE_URL_LIGHTARK / DIRECT_DATABASE_URL_LIGHTARK as its own database.
# They are NOT the product brand (that comes from the Host; see BRAND_LOCK below).
# APP_NAME=
# BRAND=
# DATABASE_URL_LIGHTARK=
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL_LIGHTARK=
# Candidate-facing posting page of each recruiter bank: an https URL that
# contains {id}. No default. Unset = that bank's jobs are synced and counted but
# not listed, because a job with no working apply link is never shown.
# These replace ROBOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_BASE_URL and GOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_BASE_URL,
# which are no longer read: the <base>/jobs/<id> page they pointed at does not
# exist on either site (both render "Page not found", checked 2026-10-11). Set a
# template only once the bank's product has a public posting page.
# ROBOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_URL_TEMPLATE=
# GOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_URL_TEMPLATE=
# How GoApply reads the GoHire bank: db | api | off. Unset: db when
# DATABASE_URL_GOHIRE satisfies the TLS rule, else api (the HTTPS list endpoint
# of GOHIRE_API_BASE) when GOHIRE_API_KEY is set, else the bank is not read.
# GOHIRE_BANK_TRANSPORT=
# GoHire syndication endpoint (https; cursor and tombstones), once it exists.
# Set: used in place of the list endpoint on the api transport. Unset (the
# default) = the list endpoint.
# GOHIRE_SYNDICATION_URL=
# GoHire resume parsing — primary extract+parse for plain PDF uploads.
# Without a key the ingest falls back to the local OCR pipeline, which is
# unreliable on image-only scans. GOHIRE_PARSE_ENABLED=false forces the fallback.
GOHIRE_API_KEY=
GOHIRE_API_BASE=https://api.gohire.top
GOHIRE_PARSE_ENABLED=true
GOHIRE_PARSE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# Which brands send PDF uploads to the GoHire parse API (a mainland server).
# Default goapply only (R-16); add roboapply only after the privacy notice
# discloses the transfer.
GOHIRE_PARSE_BRANDS=goapply
# Kill switches + tuning.
# RA_CROSSBANK_DISABLED turns off EVERY read of the recruiter banks: the legacy
# /v2/discover route AND the bank ingest adapters that fill the job list
# (raBankClients.isBankEnabled). To close only the legacy route, use
# RA_V2_DISCOVER_DISABLED below.
RA_CROSSBANK_DISABLED=false
# true → POST /api/v1/roboapply/v2/discover/run answers 404 feature_disabled on
# both brands. The route has no web caller (owner decision pending: retire or
# keep) and charges no credit, so `true` is the recommended value in every
# deployment until that decision. Unset/false keeps it served behind its gates
# (session, GoApply recruitment-info mode, phone binding, AI consent, daily cap).
RA_V2_DISCOVER_DISABLED=false
RA_CROSSBANK_ROBOHIRE_DISABLED=false
RA_CROSSBANK_GOHIRE_DISABLED=false
# Contractual white-label sign-off REQUIRED to read the FOREIGN brand's bank.
# The bank ingest is behind the same guard: on a deployment whose APP_NAME is
# not gohire (every RoboApply / GoApply deployment), GoApply's GoHire bank is
# read only with this set to true.
RA_CROSSBANK_CROSS_TENANT_CONFIRMED=false
RA_CROSSBANK_SCORER_BUDGET=16
RA_CROSSBANK_INVITE_OFFSET=0
# Model calls one user may spend on /v2/discover per UTC day (default 400).
RA_CROSSBANK_DAILY_CALL_CAP=
# Per-agent model overrides (fall back to raModels tiers).
RA_V2_CROSSBANK_EXPLORER_MODEL=
RA_V2_CROSSBANK_INSIGHT_MODEL=

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Jobright clone (feat/jobright-clone): dual brand RoboApply + GoApply
#
# Brand parity (owner ruling D5; docs/jobright-clone/GOAPPLY_PARITY_PLAN.md):
# a capability that is on for RoboApply is on for GoApply by default. GoApply
# needs NO variable of its own. With only the shared credentials above (an LLM
# key, RESEND_API_KEY, LIVEKIT_*, S3_*, VAPID_*) it has AI, email, voice
# practice, storage, web push, the job feed and open sign-up.
#
# Naming rule (server/src/platform/brand/brandEnv.ts):
#   NAME     → the shared value; RoboApply (roboapply.io, international incl.
#              Taiwan) always reads this and never a CN_ value
#   CN_NAME  → OPTIONAL override for GoApply (goapply.top, mainland China)
# For GoApply a name is read in one of three ways:
#   1. Per key (most names: LLM_*, TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY, COPILOT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD,
#      SCORE_DAILY_BUDGET, RA_SYSTEM_USER_ID, INTERVIEW_RETENTION_DAYS,
#      INTERVIEW_ENGINE_RECORDING_ENABLED, …): CN_NAME when set, else NAME.
#   2. Grouped: settings that belong together are read as ONE set, wholly from
#      CN_* when the group's anchor is set and wholly from the shared names
#      otherwise, so a URL of one account is never paired with a key of another.
#        voice    anchor CN_LIVEKIT_URL: LIVEKIT_URL, LIVEKIT_API_KEY,
#                 LIVEKIT_API_SECRET, LIVEKIT_AGENT_NAME,
#                 LIVEKIT_AGENT_CALLBACK_SECRET, VOICE_PROVIDER,
#                 INTERVIEW_ENGINE_AGENT_NAME, INTERVIEW_ENGINE_CALLBACK_BASE_URL
#        speech   anchors CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_MODEL and
#                 CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_MODEL (both must be set):
#                 INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_MODEL, INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_MODEL,
#                 INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_VOICE, INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_VOICE_MALE,
#                 INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_FALLBACK_MODELS
#        storage  anchor CN_S3_BUCKET: S3_BUCKET, S3_ENDPOINT, S3_REGION,
#                 S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID, S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE,
#                 AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_REGION
#        push     anchor CN_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY: VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY,
#                 VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, VAPID_SUBJECT
#      A group follows its anchor: without it the other CN_ values of the group
#      are ignored (startup names them in a warning); with it a missing member
#      is simply unset and is never taken from the shared set.
#   3. Brand-own (identity never crosses brands): CN_NAME only, never the shared
#      value. CANONICAL_ORIGIN, COOKIE_DOMAIN, BACKEND_URL, EMAIL_FROM,
#      SUPPORT_EMAIL, COACHING_ADMIN_EMAIL, TAKEDOWN_CONTACT, LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME,
#      LEGAL_POSTAL_ADDRESS, LEGAL_DOCS_VERSION, PAYMENT_COLLECTING_ENTITY,
#      MIN_EXT_VERSION, BAIDU_PUSH_TOKEN, CONTACT_OPTIN_API_URL,
#      CONTACT_OPTIN_API_KEY, CONTENT_SAFETY_PROVIDER, CONTENT_SAFETY_TIMEOUT_MS,
#      SAFETY_KEYWORDS_URL. Each has a safe default when unset (the registry
#      origin, no legal line printed, the built-in keyword list).
# Vendor-only keys stay unprefixed (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, WECHAT_*, ALIYUN_*).
#
# What differs per brand by design: job sources and job-search providers,
# language, currency, prices, the payment rail (Alipay for GoApply, Stripe for
# RoboApply), extra sign-in methods and legal lines.
#
# Off switches for GoApply (each capability is on when its switch is unset):
#   the job feed          CN_RECRUITMENT_INFO_MODE=off
#   the campus calendar   CN_CAMPUS_CALENDAR_ENABLED=false
#   open sign-up          CN_SIGNUP_MODE=invite or closed
#   charging              CN_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=false
#   email                 CN_EMAIL_TRANSPORT=none
#   camera and video      CN_INTERVIEW_CAMERA_PUBLISH=false
#   one capability        FLAG_GOAPPLY_<KEY>=false
# The strict mainland posture is an explicit choice, never the result of a
# missing value: CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT, CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY, CN_STORAGE_MODE.
#
# Every variable below is optional. Values are owner-supplied (OPS track);
# never commit real ones.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Brand resolution and deployment scope ───────────────────────────────────
# Brands this deployment serves: roboapply, goapply (or intl, cn), comma list.
# Unset: BOTH brands, in every environment, production included. So a production
# deployment serves goapply.top as soon as its DNS points at it. To keep GoApply
# closed set ALLOWED_BRANDS=roboapply; the mainland kit sets ALLOWED_BRANDS=goapply.
# A value that names no valid brand (a typo such as "roboaply") is not treated
# as unset: the deployment then serves RoboApply only, and startup logs the bad
# value. It does not refuse to boot (on the mainland kit it does, because
# RoboApply is not allowed there).
ALLOWED_BRANDS=
# Pin every request to one brand (single-brand deployments). A value that names
# no valid brand follows the same rule as ALLOWED_BRANDS.
BRAND_LOCK=
# Extra host → brand pairs, e.g. staging.goapply.top=goapply,pr-1.vercel.app=goapply
BRAND_HOST_MAP=
# Dev/preview hosts only: force a brand (the ?__brand= cookie also works there).
BRAND_FORCE=
# Shared secret that lets Next.js server code send x-ra-brand to the API on a
# production host (header x-ra-internal). Must be IDENTICAL on the API and web
# sides: it also gates /api/revalidate and is required before the API trusts
# x-ra-client-ip from the web server (WP-56).
INTERNAL_API_SECRET=
# Server-only API origin for server-rendered reads (SEO, campus pages). Set it
# where the production host is neither a registry brand host nor a
# BRAND_HOST_MAP entry; otherwise those pages load their lists client-side
# (WP-58). A local `next start` reads NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, falling back to
# http://localhost:4607, never the live site (WP-56).
INTERNAL_API_ORIGIN=
# cn-mainland marks a deployment inside mainland China (the deploy/cn kit);
# unset elsewhere. There the startup check refuses to boot only on topology:
# an unknown region, no database URL, a database host outside the allowlist, or
# RoboApply being served. A missing ICP number, a model route outside the
# mainland, no mainland bucket, content safety that is not Aliyun Green and an
# offshore email transport are logged as warnings and GoApply runs on the
# shared stack. The region alone no longer decides GoApply's storage rule, its
# egress rule, the cross-border consent or whether its free tools are open:
# those follow the stack in use (and the strict switch below).
DEPLOY_REGION=
# Comma list of DB host suffixes allowed when DEPLOY_REGION=cn-mainland.
CN_ALLOWED_DB_HOST_SUFFIXES=
# Strict mainland posture (default off). true = GoApply personal data may go
# only to mainland endpoints (the egress allowlist applies), a mainland bucket
# is required (uploads are refused without CN_S3_*), the warnings above become
# boot failures, a half-set CN_S3_* group (in every region, not only on the
# mainland) and an invalid content-safety setting fail instead of falling
# back, and CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY is implied. Set it only when the domestic
# providers below are configured.
# CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT=false
# Canonical origins for email links, SEO and OAuth redirects.
CANONICAL_ORIGIN=https://www.roboapply.io
CN_CANONICAL_ORIGIN=https://www.goapply.top
# GoApply session-cookie domain (COOKIE_DOMAIN above is RoboApply's).
# CN_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.goapply.top
# Per-brand capability overrides: FLAG_<BRAND>_<KEY>=on|off (or a mode). A
# capability is on when its own requirement is met AND this override (else the
# registry default) says on. The registry default is on for both brands for
# coaching, the extension, voice practice, web push and student prices, so on
# GoApply the override is an off switch, e.g.
#   FLAG_GOAPPLY_COACHING=false          FLAG_GOAPPLY_INTERVIEW_VOICE=false
#   FLAG_GOAPPLY_WEB_PUSH=false          FLAG_GOAPPLY_STUDENT=false
#   FLAG_GOAPPLY_COPILOT=false           FLAG_GOAPPLY_EXTENSION=false
#   FLAG_GOAPPLY_AUTH_PHONE_OTP=false   (phone sign-in off even with an SMS
#                                        provider; then no account is asked to
#                                        bind a phone before using AI)
# Off by default on both brands; =true turns one on (the FLAG_ROBOAPPLY_ twins
# work the same way): FLAG_GOAPPLY_VISITOR_ASSISTANT (the assistant for
# signed-out visitors), FLAG_GOAPPLY_COMPANY_NEWS and FLAG_GOAPPLY_SEO_BROWSE
# (the public browse pages; public job pages do not depend on it).
# A mode flag takes its mode:
#   FLAG_ROBOAPPLY_HIRING_CONTACTS=off|deeplinks_only|on
# System user for system-owned records. GoApply: CN_RA_SYSTEM_USER_ID when set,
# else RA_SYSTEM_USER_ID.
RA_SYSTEM_USER_ID=
CN_RA_SYSTEM_USER_ID=
# Baidu site verification meta (GoApply only; read by app/layout.tsx).
BAIDU_SITE_VERIFICATION=
CN_BAIDU_PUSH_TOKEN=

# ── Auth (both brands) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# LINE Login (Taiwan); apply for the email permission.
LINE_LOGIN_CHANNEL_ID=
LINE_LOGIN_CHANNEL_SECRET=
# AES key for sensitive profile answers (EEO / CN sensitive fields).
SENSITIVE_DATA_KEY=
# Key rotation (WP-19): version stamped on new ciphertexts (default 1) and the
# previous key, still accepted for reads until every row is re-encrypted.
SENSITIVE_DATA_KEY_VERSION=
SENSITIVE_DATA_KEY_PREVIOUS=

# ── Auth (GoApply) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Email + password is the primary sign-in method on both brands and needs
# nothing here. Phone OTP and WeChat are ADDITIONAL GoApply methods: each
# appears beside email only when its credentials below are set. Google and LINE
# stay RoboApply's additional methods (a market difference).
# GoApply sign-up: open | invite | closed. Default open (anyone can sign up
# with email and password). invite = a new account needs an invite code;
# closed = no new accounts. Any other value is read as open and reported as a
# mistake.
# CN_SIGNUP_MODE=open
# Optional: SMS OTP provider for phone sign-in, aliyun | tencent. Unset = no
# phone tab. SMS_DEV_CONSOLE=true (never read in production) prints the codes
# in the API log instead, for a local demo of phone sign-in.
CN_SMS_PROVIDER=
SMS_DEV_CONSOLE=
SMS_DAILY_MAX=
ALIYUN_SMS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
ALIYUN_SMS_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=
ALIYUN_SMS_SIGN_NAME=
ALIYUN_SMS_TEMPLATE_OTP=
TENCENT_SMS_SECRET_ID=
TENCENT_SMS_SECRET_KEY=
TENCENT_SMS_SDK_APP_ID=
TENCENT_SMS_SIGN_NAME=
TENCENT_SMS_TEMPLATE_OTP=
# Optional: WeChat Open Platform website app (QR login; ICP-filed domain).
# Unset = no WeChat sign-in button.
WECHAT_OPEN_APP_ID=
WECHAT_OPEN_APP_SECRET=
# Optional: WeChat 服务号 (in-WeChat login + notices; bound to the Open Platform
# for UnionID). WeChat notices are an extra GoApply channel beside email, the
# in-app inbox and web push.
WECHAT_MP_APP_ID=
WECHAT_MP_APP_SECRET=
WECHAT_MP_TOKEN=
WECHAT_MP_ENCODING_AES_KEY=
# 订阅通知 template ids (WP-73). A template with no id never sends. A value may
# also map the template's keywords: `id|keyword:source,…`; without a mapping
# DEFAULT_TEMPLATE_FIELDS in features/notify-cn/config.ts applies. Sources:
#   deadline: program, company, closesAt, days · report: title, completedAt ·
#   payment: planName, amount, paidAt, orderNo
WECHAT_MP_TEMPLATE_DEADLINE=
# Needed for the "practice report is ready" notice (live and written practice).
WECHAT_MP_TEMPLATE_REPORT=
WECHAT_MP_TEMPLATE_PAYMENT=
# WeChat mini program (P2; login API seam only).
WECHAT_MINI_APP_ID=
WECHAT_MINI_APP_SECRET=

# ── LLM routing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# New RoboApply tasks (unset → LLM_MODEL).
LLM_COPILOT_MODEL=
LLM_ENRICH_MODEL=
LLM_WRITING_MODEL=
# Optional task models read for GoApply when the CN_ twin below is unset
# (RoboApply does not use them): the campus-calendar extractor and the fraud
# second opinion. Unset = the enrichment model, then the default model.
# LLM_CAMPUS_MODEL=
# LLM_FRAUD_MODEL=
LLM_COPILOT_REASONING_EFFORT=
LLM_ENRICH_REASONING_EFFORT=
LLM_WRITING_REASONING_EFFORT=
# Extra max_tokens added only when a vendor's thinking mode is explicitly on.
LLM_THINKING_HEADROOM_TOKENS=
# Providers OpenRouter must not route RoboApply prompts to (comma list). Can only
# ADD to the built-in mainland exclusion list (deepseek, alibaba, baidu,
# streamlake), never remove from it (WP-14).
OPENROUTER_IGNORE_PROVIDERS=
# GoApply models: OPTIONAL overrides; unset = shared stack. With none of these
# set GoApply uses the same provider, models and fallback chain as RoboApply
# (LLM_PROVIDER, LLM_MODEL and the task settings above). Each setting resolves
# per key: the admin override for GoApply, then CN_<NAME>, then the admin
# override for RoboApply, then <NAME>. GoApply has "its own LLM stack" once
# CN_LLM_PROVIDER or CN_LLM_MODEL is set (domestic vendors: deepseek,
# qwen/dashscope, kimi, glm, doubao/ark, minimax); a setting that still comes
# from the shared stack then keeps its shared route, it is never sent to the
# CN provider. GoApply prompts always pass the content-safety filter below.
# `npm run verify:llm` prints, per brand and per task, the stack each model
# setting resolves to and the variable it really comes from ([own] or
# [shared]). Without --probe it calls no provider.
CN_LLM_PROVIDER=
CN_LLM_MODEL=
# true = GoApply may call mainland model endpoints only: primary and fallback
# routes, a user's own key, and the enrichment, campus and fraud models. It
# then needs a route on a mainland endpoint (normally CN_LLM_PROVIDER and
# CN_LLM_MODEL) for GoApply AI to work. Default off. Implied by the strict
# posture (CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT=true).
# CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY=false
CN_LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=
CN_LLM_MATCHING_MODEL=
CN_LLM_EXTRACT_MODEL=
CN_LLM_ONBOARDING_MODEL=
CN_LLM_REWRITE_MODEL=
CN_LLM_INTERVIEW_MODEL=
CN_LLM_COPILOT_MODEL=
CN_LLM_ENRICH_MODEL=
# GoApply fraud second opinion (WP-41); unset = LLM_FRAUD_MODEL, then the
# enrichment model, then the default model, through the shared resolver. A
# domestic provider is required only under CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY.
CN_LLM_FRAUD_MODEL=
CN_LLM_WRITING_MODEL=
# GoApply campus-calendar extractor (WP-58, optional); unset =
# LLM_CAMPUS_MODEL, then the enrichment model, then the default model. A
# domestic provider is required only under CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY.
CN_LLM_CAMPUS_MODEL=
# Unset = LLM_VISION_MODEL, then the default model (ai.vision follows ai.text).
CN_LLM_VISION_MODEL=
# On DEPLOY_REGION=cn-mainland the startup check also looks at any
# CN_RA_MODEL_<AGENT> value that is set: a route outside the mainland is a
# warning, and a boot failure under CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT. Nothing else reads
# those names today.
# Run batch jobs in the vendors' off-peak window (true|false).
CN_LLM_OFFPEAK_BATCH=
# Off-peak windows for GoApply batch jobs, Beijing time, comma list, e.g. "00:30-08:30" (WP-14 offPeak.ts).
CN_LLM_OFFPEAK_WINDOWS=
# Extra mainland hosts a self-hosted `newapi` gateway may use (comma list).
# Only consulted under CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_ONLY (or the strict posture).
CN_LLM_DOMESTIC_HOSTS=
# Domestic vendor keys (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is above).
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
DASHSCOPE_BASE_URL=
KIMI_API_KEY=
GLM_API_KEY=
GLM_API_BASE_URL=
ARK_API_KEY=
ARK_BASE_URL=
# Vendor thinking switches (on|off; unset = vendor default).
DASHSCOPE_THINKING_MODE=
GLM_THINKING_MODE=
ARK_THINKING_MODE=
MINIMAX_API_KEY=
# Assistant daily spend guard (USD). GoApply: CN_COPILOT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD when
# set, else COPILOT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD.
COPILOT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=
CN_COPILOT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=

# ── GoApply generative-AI content safety (WP-24) ────────────────────────────
# The filter runs on every GoApply model call, on the shared route too, and
# needs no setting: the default is keyword_only with the built-in list.
# keyword_only | aliyun_green. An invalid value here (or an invalid timeout or
# keyword URL) falls back to keyword_only with a warning, so it never turns
# GoApply AI off; it fails closed only under CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT. On a
# mainland deployment (DEPLOY_REGION=cn-mainland) anything other than
# aliyun_green with its keys is a warning (a boot failure under
# CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT).
# CN_CONTENT_SAFETY_PROVIDER=keyword_only
ALIYUN_GREEN_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
ALIYUN_GREEN_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=
# Private keyword list location (optional; unset = the built-in list).
CN_SAFETY_KEYWORDS_URL=
# Check timeout in ms (default 5000, allowed 500–30000). A check that times out
# fails closed (503).
CN_CONTENT_SAFETY_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Mainland region only (default cn-shanghai); optional mainland green-cip host.
ALIYUN_GREEN_REGION=
ALIYUN_GREEN_ENDPOINT=
# Large-model moderation services (defaults llm_query_moderation / llm_response_moderation).
ALIYUN_GREEN_INPUT_SERVICE=
ALIYUN_GREEN_OUTPUT_SERVICE=

# ── Job inventory, enrichment and scoring ───────────────────────────────────
# Job sources are the one thing that differs per brand by design (D5, D6):
#   RoboApply  activejobs, jsearch (RapidAPI), the RoboHire bank, public
#              employer boards (postings outside mainland China), user imports.
#              The LinkedIn feed is not a source (not subscribed, not to be).
#   GoApply    public employer boards (postings located in mainland China; this
#              is what fills the feed), the GoHire bank (synced; listed only
#              with GOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_URL_TEMPLATE), user imports, the campus
#              calendar. JSearch is not a GoApply source and no RapidAPI call
#              is made for GoApply. No mainland board is ever scraped.
# Narrow a brand's ingest providers: comma list, a SUBSET of the brand's
# registry list (a name outside it is ignored). Unset = the whole list.
# JOB_PROVIDERS_ROBOAPPLY=
# JOB_PROVIDERS_GOAPPLY=
# Daily call budget per metered ingest provider (INGEST_<PROVIDER>_DAILY_CALLS).
INGEST_ACTIVEJOBS_DAILY_CALLS=
INGEST_JSEARCH_DAILY_CALLS=
# Ingest tuning (WP-16b): queries leased per run, SEO seed plan, bank page size.
INGEST_LEASE_BATCH=
INGEST_SEED_ROLES=
INGEST_SEED_CITIES_PER_COUNTRY=
INGEST_SEED_COUNTRIES=
# Share of each provider's daily calls SEO seed queries may use (default 0.5).
INGEST_SEED_BUDGET_SHARE=
INGEST_BANK_PAGE=
ENRICH_DAILY_JOBS=
SCORE_DAILY_BUDGET=
CN_SCORE_DAILY_BUDGET=
SCORE_PRECOMPUTE_PER_USER_DAY=
# Providers whose postings may appear on public SEO pages (owner decision):
# comma list of activejobs, jsearch, ats_public. Default empty: only recruiter
# bank jobs with syndication consent have a public page. The same gate on both
# brands: GoApply's public job pages, ticker and sitemap partitions follow it
# too (its employer-board postings need ats_public here), and the seo-rebuild
# cron runs for GoApply. The browse pages also need FLAG_<BRAND>_SEO_BROWSE=true
# (off by default).
PUBLIC_DISPLAY_PROVIDERS=
# Fetch provider for "import a job from a link" (both brands). On a mainland
# deployment (DEPLOY_REGION=cn-mainland) a link import that cannot use it (no
# key, refused by the residency policy, or CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT) reads the page
# once from the server instead, and falls back to pasting the text when the
# page cannot be read. Elsewhere the fallback is paste only.
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# Fit weights (JSON, title_level/skills/industry/logistics/career_path) and
# tier thresholds (JSON, great/good/possible); defaults 35/30/15/10/10, 80/65/45.
MATCH_WEIGHTS=
MATCH_TIERS=
# Hosts the job-import fetcher refuses (comma list; added to the built-in list).
IMPORT_FETCH_DENYLIST=
# Public ATS job boards (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, SmartRecruiters; WP-42),
# read through their documented job-board APIs for both brands. A posting's
# market follows its own location: mainland China → GoApply, anything else →
# RoboApply. Kill switch: true stops every board read (and empties the GoApply
# feed, whose listed postings come from these boards). Default off (boards are read).
ATS_PUBLIC_SOURCES_DISABLED=
# Taiwan open data (licence pending verification; WP-42 stub stays off).
TW_OPEN_DATA_JOBS_ENABLED=
TW_OPEN_DATA_JOBS_URL=
# GoApply recruitment-information mode: off | partner_deeplink | licensed.
# Default licensed: the job feed, recommendations and alerts are ON when this
# is unset. `off` is the off switch, and only the literal word off closes the
# feed: any other value (false, 0, a typo) is read as licensed and startup
# logs it as a mistake. partner_deeplink sends every apply through the
# partner's page. off also closes GoApply's job search, its public job and
# browse pages, the ticker and the sitemap partitions, and skips its
# seo-rebuild run.
# CN_RECRUITMENT_INFO_MODE=licensed
# Campus calendar (official links only). On by default; false hides it.
# CN_CAMPUS_CALENDAR_ENABLED=true

# ── Credits and plans (R-07, R-08; prices per market, D6) ───────────────────
# Plan keys: PRO_WEEKLY, PRO_MONTHLY, PRO_QUARTERLY, PRO_WEEK_PASS,
# PRACTICE_PACK_5, PRACTICE_PACK_15, STUDENT_MONTHLY, STUDENT_QUARTERLY.
# RoboApply (Stripe, USD): a plan is sellable when its Stripe price is set:
# STRIPE_PRICE_<PLANKEY>=price_… and STRIPE_PRICE_<PLANKEY>_CENTS=<display amount>
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_WEEKLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_WEEKLY_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_QUARTERLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_QUARTERLY_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_WEEK_PASS=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_WEEK_PASS_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_PACK_5=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_PACK_5_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_PACK_15=
STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_PACK_15_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDENT_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDENT_MONTHLY_CENTS=
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDENT_QUARTERLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDENT_QUARTERLY_CENTS=
# Taiwan (WP-79, TW-06): real TWD prices per plan, e.g.
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY_TWD=price_… and STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY_TWD_CENTS=74900
# (NT$749). Both set → Taiwan sees the TWD price; otherwise the USD price with
# the reference line.
# Extra school email domains for student prices, comma list (besides .edu,
# .edu.<cc>, .ac.<cc>, which already cover .edu.cn), e.g. "ethz.ch,tum.de".
# Student verification and student prices run on both brands.
STUDENT_EMAIL_DOMAINS=
# Two-step sign-in (TOTP) secret sealing key, 32 bytes as base64 or 64 hex
# chars. GoApply: CN_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY when set, else TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY;
# opening a stored secret tries both, so adding the CN key later locks nobody
# out. Keep TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY in the GoApply environment after adding the CN
# key: without it, accounts enrolled before the change can sign in only with a
# recovery code. Neither set → two-step sign-in unavailable.
TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
CN_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# GoApply (one-time passes and packs, CNY, paid through Alipay): purchasable
# by default. The plan catalog carries the amounts, so no price variable is
# needed and no GoApply plan is ever "price not set":
#   PRO_WEEK_PASS ¥12 · PRO_MONTHLY ¥39 · PRO_QUARTERLY ¥99 ·
#   PRACTICE_PACK_5 ¥29 · PRACTICE_PACK_15 ¥79 ·
#   STUDENT_MONTHLY ¥29 · STUDENT_QUARTERLY ¥69
# Opening a payment also needs the rail's own credential (ALIPAY_CALLBACK_SECRET
# above); without it the plans and prices still show.
# Kill switch: false (or 0 / off / no) stops GoApply charging on both CN rails
# (no new order can be opened). The Alipay callback, the WeChat Pay notify and
# the order status stay open, so an order that was already paid is still
# credited. Unset = on.
# CN_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true
# Optional override of a catalog amount, in fen. Whole yuan only (a multiple of
# 100, because the payment worker bills whole yuan): any other value is ignored
# and logged, and the catalog default applies. Applies to new orders only.
CN_PRICE_PRO_WEEK_PASS_FEN=
CN_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY_FEN=
CN_PRICE_PRO_QUARTERLY_FEN=
CN_PRICE_PRACTICE_PACK_5_FEN=
CN_PRICE_PRACTICE_PACK_15_FEN=
CN_PRICE_STUDENT_MONTHLY_FEN=
CN_PRICE_STUDENT_QUARTERLY_FEN=
# true → skip the AppConfig credits.catalog.v1 override (code defaults only).
CREDITS_CATALOG_DB_DISABLED=
# Show Stripe promotion-code entry at checkout (default off; no offers at launch).
STRIPE_PROMOTION_CODES=
# GoApply: the legal entity that collects payments. Brand-own and optional:
# when set it is printed on the order description (body) and the receipt; the
# order subject is unchanged. When unset the Alipay order is created without it
# and startup logs one warning. The Alipay merchant should be the GoApply
# operating entity (no 二清).
CN_PAYMENT_COLLECTING_ENTITY=
# true = the Alipay rail refuses to charge until CN_PAYMENT_COLLECTING_ENTITY
# is set (the former hard gate). Default off.
# CN_PAYMENT_REQUIRE_ENTITY=false
# GoApply Alipay platform id at the payment worker (unset = gohire), and the
# origin the worker posts the callback to (brand-own; unset = GoApply's
# canonical origin, never BACKEND_URL).
CN_ALIPAY_PLATFORM=
CN_BACKEND_URL=
# Alipay through the GoHire worker today (ALIPAY_API_URL / ALIPAY_CALLBACK_SECRET above).
ROBOAPPLY_ALIPAY_PLATFORM=
# WeChat Pay merchant (APIv3): GoApply's second, optional rail. It appears only
# with the whole merchant set below and a matching entity; Alipay does not
# depend on it.
WECHATPAY_MCH_ID=
WECHATPAY_APP_ID=
WECHATPAY_API_V3_KEY=
WECHATPAY_MCH_CERT_SERIAL=
WECHATPAY_MCH_PRIVATE_KEY=
WECHATPAY_PUBLIC_KEY_ID=
WECHATPAY_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Must be a GoApply host (as must CN_BACKEND_URL when it carries the notify path).
WECHATPAY_NOTIFY_URL=
# Legal name the WeChat Pay merchant account is registered to; must match
# CN_PAYMENT_COLLECTING_ENTITY or WeChat Pay stays off (WP-62; Alipay is not
# affected). WeChat Pay checkout also needs CN_LEGAL_DOCS_VERSION (the 用户协议
# version the order records).
WECHATPAY_MERCHANT_ENTITY=

# ── Email and notifications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GoApply email transport: OPTIONAL override; unset = shared stack.
# aliyun_dm | resend | none. Default resend (the shared RESEND_API_KEY), so
# verification mail, password reset and alerts work with nothing set here.
# aliyun_dm needs the ALIYUN_DM_* keys below; none turns GoApply email off.
# CN_EMAIL_TRANSPORT=resend
# GoApply sender address (brand-own, optional). Unset with Resend: the shared
# verified sender (ROBOAPPLY_EMAIL_FROM, then EMAIL_FROM) under the display
# name GoApply, because noreply@goapply.top is not a verified domain on the
# shared account. Set it once a goapply.top sender is verified. With
# aliyun_dm the shared sender is never borrowed. Reply-To and the legal lines
# of a GoApply mail always come from GoApply's own values.
CN_EMAIL_FROM=
ALIYUN_DM_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
ALIYUN_DM_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=
ALIYUN_DM_ACCOUNT_NAME=
ALIYUN_DM_REGION=
# Signs one-click unsubscribe links (unset → derived from JWT_SECRET).
EMAIL_UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET=
# Reply-To for system mail.
SUPPORT_EMAIL=
CN_SUPPORT_EMAIL=
# Address the legal documents give for takedown notices (API and web legal
# pages); unset → SUPPORT_EMAIL / CN_SUPPORT_EMAIL.
TAKEDOWN_CONTACT=
CN_TAKEDOWN_CONTACT=
# Staff copy of coaching requests (WP-72); unset → SUPPORT_EMAIL / CN_SUPPORT_EMAIL.
COACHING_ADMIN_EMAIL=
CN_COACHING_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# Invite-reward risk signal hashes (WP-60); unset → derived from JWT_SECRET.
# With neither set in production no signals are stored and every qualified
# invite is held for review.
REFERRAL_SIGNAL_SECRET=
# Comma list notified of operational alerts.
ADMIN_ALERT_EMAILS=
# Web push (both brands). The `webPush` capability is on only with BOTH keys
# and a VAPID_SUBJECT that is a `mailto:` or `https:` URL; otherwise the push
# routes answer 404.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:support@roboapply.io
# GoApply's own VAPID pair: OPTIONAL override; unset = shared stack (the pair
# above). One group, anchored on CN_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY: set it and the private
# key and subject are read from CN_VAPID_* only; without it the other two are
# ignored. An own set must be complete: the public key alone turns GoApply web
# push off.
CN_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
CN_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
CN_VAPID_SUBJECT=
# Lifecycle mail "your resume check is ready" (row 4): ISO time the
# resume-check view stamp (RAResumeGrade.viewedAt) went live in this
# environment, e.g. 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z. Only checks completed on or after it
# count as "unopened". Unset or unreadable = that message is never sent.
RESUME_CHECK_VIEW_SIGNAL_SINCE=

# ── Legal display (footer, privacy notice) — shown only when set ────────────
# Brand-own: GoApply prints only its own lines, each only when set, and never
# RoboApply's entity. None of them is needed for GoApply to work.
LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME=
LEGAL_POSTAL_ADDRESS=
CN_LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME=
CN_LEGAL_POSTAL_ADDRESS=
CN_ICP_NUMBER=
CN_PSB_NUMBER=
CN_PSB_RECORD_CODE=
CN_EDI_LICENCE_NUMBER=
CN_HR_LICENCE_NUMBER=
CN_HR_LICENCE_HOLDER=
# JSON [{ "model", "vendor", "filingNo" }]
CN_GENAI_DISCLOSURES=
CN_GENAI_APP_REGISTRATION_NO=
CN_ALGORITHM_FILING_NO=
# Shown only when set; nothing reads "备案中" otherwise.
CN_GENAI_STATUS_NOTE=
CN_COMPLAINT_EMAIL=
CN_COMPLAINT_PHONE=
# Version of GoApply's counsel-approved legal documents, recorded with
# consents. Unset: the documents are still served, as drafts with the DRAFT
# banner, exactly as on RoboApply, and sign-up stays open.
CN_LEGAL_DOCS_VERSION=
# RoboApply legal documents version (recorded with consents; WP-13).
LEGAL_DOCS_VERSION=
# Optional override of the content/legal directory.
LEGAL_CONTENT_DIR=
# Neon point-in-time history window, shown in the retention table. Set it to the
# real value before publishing the privacy notices ("Not listed" while unset).
BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=
# Explicit "AI-generated" footer line on GoApply exports (true|false).
CN_AI_EXPORT_EXPLICIT_LABEL=

# ── Storage (GoApply) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GoApply's own bucket: OPTIONAL override; unset = shared stack. Without
# CN_S3_BUCKET GoApply uses the shared store (S3_* above): resume originals
# and photos under a goapply/ key prefix, practice recordings and transcripts
# beside RoboApply's. With CN_S3_BUCKET its files go to that bucket under a
# cn/ key prefix. Uploads are refused for a missing CN bucket only under the
# strict posture (CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT=true).
# Moving to an own bucket later: GoApply practice recordings made before the
# change stay in the shared bucket. They are still deleted on time, but their
# playback links stop (the report shows no recording). Copy the
# interviews/<sessionId>/ objects across if they should stay playable.
# One group, anchored on CN_S3_BUCKET: set it and every other storage value is
# read from CN_* only (a missing key is unset, never the shared key); without
# it the other CN_S3_* / CN_AWS_* values are ignored.
# CN_S3_BUCKET must differ from S3_BUCKET only when both use the same endpoint
# (the same bucket name on two different endpoints is two buckets).
CN_S3_ENDPOINT=
CN_S3_REGION=
CN_S3_BUCKET=
CN_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CN_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
CN_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=
# Aliases read when the CN_S3_* key pair is unset (same group; WP-63a).
CN_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CN_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
CN_AWS_REGION=
# What GoApply keeps of an uploaded resume: store | redact | discard.
# Default store (the original file and the text as written, as on RoboApply).
# redact = identity numbers and health details are removed from the stored
# text and fields; the uploaded file is still kept. discard = no original file
# and no photo is kept, and the stored text is redacted. Any other value is
# read as discard and startup logs it as a mistake (a typo in a privacy switch
# never keeps more than intended).
# CN_STORAGE_MODE=store
# https origin GoApply's public images are served from (OSS bucket or CDN, with
# an optional base path). Build-time: next.config.mjs turns it into the one
# extra host next/image may load; anything that is not a plain https URL of a
# real host is ignored.
CN_PUBLIC_ASSET_BASE_URL=
# Extra mainland object-storage host suffixes accepted as in-region (comma list;
# Aliyun oss-cn-*, Tencent COS mainland and Huawei obs.cn-* are built in). Used
# by the mainland storage check (a warning, or a failure under CN_RESIDENCY_STRICT).
CN_ALLOWED_STORAGE_HOST_SUFFIXES=

# ── Interview voice (GoApply) and retention ─────────────────────────────────
# GoApply's own media plane: OPTIONAL override; unset = shared stack. Without
# CN_LIVEKIT_URL GoApply voice and video practice runs on the shared LiveKit
# project (LIVEKIT_* above), the shared worker and its agent name
# (INTERVIEW_ENGINE_AGENT_NAME), with the shared zh voices and speech models,
# and its artifacts go to the storage group above.
# One group, anchored on CN_LIVEKIT_URL: set it and the key, secret, callback
# secret, callback base URL, agent name and CN_VOICE_PROVIDER are read from
# CN_* only; without it those CN_ values are ignored. A session keeps the
# plane it started on.
CN_LIVEKIT_URL=
CN_LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
CN_LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
CN_LIVEKIT_AGENT_CALLBACK_SECRET=
# Not used for dispatch (see LIVEKIT_AGENT_NAME above); leave unset.
CN_LIVEKIT_AGENT_NAME=
# The name a worker on GoApply's OWN plane registers under and is dispatched
# by (GoApply-Interview when unset there). Set it only together with
# CN_LIVEKIT_URL: on the shared plane nobody registers that name.
# CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_AGENT_NAME=GoApply-Interview
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_CALLBACK_BASE_URL=
# Recording: CN value when set, else INTERVIEW_ENGINE_RECORDING_ENABLED above
# (off unless true). Recorded only with the user's per-session consent.
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_RECORDING_ENABLED=
# Camera and video recording on GoApply: the same policy as RoboApply (camera
# published, video recorded only with the per-session recording and video
# consents). false = audio-only practice on GoApply: the camera stays a local
# preview and no video is recorded. Default on.
# CN_INTERVIEW_CAMERA_PUBLISH=true
# livekit_cloud | livekit_selfhosted (volcano / trtc are reserved and answer 503).
# CN_VOICE_PROVIDER belongs to the voice group (read only with CN_LIVEKIT_URL).
VOICE_PROVIDER=
CN_VOICE_PROVIDER=
# GoApply live-interview models: OPTIONAL overrides; unset = RoboApply's
# interview routing (LLM_INTERVIEW_* above, the same ALIGNED_INTERVIEW_MODELS
# allowlist). A domestic live model is sent as written only on GoApply's own
# media plane (CN_LIVEKIT_URL); on the shared plane the value must be a model
# the shared worker can run (a LiveKit Inference id).
CN_LLM_INTERVIEW_LIVE_MODEL=
CN_LLM_INTERVIEW_LIVE_REASONING_EFFORT=
CN_LLM_INTERVIEW_BLUEPRINT_MODEL=
# GoApply's own speech models: one group, anchored on BOTH the STT and the TTS
# model (e.g. dashscope/paraformer-realtime-v2 and dashscope/cosyvoice-v2).
# With only one of the two set, all five are ignored and the shared voice
# catalog and speech models are used.
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_MODEL=
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_MODEL=
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_STT_FALLBACK_MODELS=
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_VOICE=
CN_INTERVIEW_ENGINE_TTS_VOICE_MALE=
# Days recordings and transcripts are kept before the purge (default 90).
# GoApply: CN_INTERVIEW_RETENTION_DAYS when set, else INTERVIEW_RETENTION_DAYS.
INTERVIEW_RETENTION_DAYS=90
CN_INTERVIEW_RETENTION_DAYS=
# A worker for GoApply's OWN media plane (domestic backends) reads WORKER_BRAND,
# LLM_BACKEND, LLM_BASE_URL, LLM_API_KEY, LLM_MODEL, STT_BACKEND, TTS_BACKEND,
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY and COSYVOICE_VOICE_ZH_{FEMALE,MALE} from its own
# environment, not from here: interview-agent/.env.local in dev, the Secret
# `goapply-worker-env` on the mainland stack (names in
# interview-agent/deploy/cn/worker.env.example). On the shared plane the one
# shared worker serves both brands and none of this is needed.

# ── Extension ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The extension is on for both brands (off switch: FLAG_<BRAND>_EXTENSION=false).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CN_EXT_ID is GoApply's Microsoft Edge Add-ons id. With no id the
# GoApply extension entry, the install link and the Devices section stay hidden.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CN_EXT_ID=
MIN_EXT_VERSION=
CN_MIN_EXT_VERSION=
# Store listing links on /extension (optional; WP-55a). GoApply: unset = the
# Microsoft Edge Add-ons listing of NEXT_PUBLIC_CN_EXT_ID.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXT_STORE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CN_EXT_STORE_URL=

# ── Integrations ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Recruiter opt-in API (RoboHire / GoHire) read by the contacts-sync cron
# (WP-54, OPS-A10). Unset → no hiring contacts are synced or shown.
CONTACT_OPTIN_API_URL=
CONTACT_OPTIN_API_KEY=
CN_CONTACT_OPTIN_API_URL=
CN_CONTACT_OPTIN_API_KEY=

# ── Platform plumbing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rate-limit overrides (JSON keyed by limit name; server/src/platform/ratelimit/defaults.ts).
RATE_LIMITS_JSON=
# Turn off every node-cron mirror of the platform crons on an always-on host;
# override one schedule with ROBOAPPLY_<NAME>_CRON (e.g. ROBOAPPLY_QUEUE_DRAIN_CRON).
ROBOAPPLY_PLATFORM_CRON_DISABLED=
# CI secrets for the mainland deploy kit (WP-76), not read by the app:
# ALIYUN_ACR_REGISTRY, ALIYUN_ACR_USERNAME, ALIYUN_ACR_PASSWORD, ACK_KUBECONFIG_B64.
#
# Build-time values of the mainland web image (read by `next build`, passed as
# build arguments by .github/workflows/deploy-cn.yml; a runtime value has no effect):
#   CN_PUBLIC_ASSET_BASE_URL (above)  the one extra host next/image may load
#   NEXT_DEPLOYMENT_ID                the git SHA; version-skew detection across web pods
#
# Names that are no longer read (delete them from an existing .env):
#   CN_EXTERNAL_PROVIDERS            ignored with one warning. JSearch is not a
#                                    GoApply source; narrow a brand's providers
#                                    with JOB_PROVIDERS_<BRAND> instead.
#   GOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_BASE_URL,
#   ROBOHIRE_PUBLIC_JOB_BASE_URL     ignored with one warning; replaced by the
#                                    *_PUBLIC_JOB_URL_TEMPLATE names above.
#   GOAPPLY_PREVIEW                  scripts/dev-clone.sh only; GoApply needs no
#                                    preview profile any more.
#   INGEST_LINKEDIN_DAILY_CALLS      the LinkedIn feed is not an ingest source of
#                                    either brand, so its budget is never read.
# Values that changed meaning: older versions of this file shipped three lines
# that are off switches now (CN_SIGNUP_MODE=invite, CN_RECRUITMENT_INFO_MODE=off
# and CN_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=false). Copied into an existing .env they still
# switch that GoApply capability off. Remove the line to get the default (on).
#
# Set by the platform or the test runner, never by hand (read, not configured):
#   VERCEL, VERCEL_ENV, VERCEL_URL, VERCEL_BRANCH_URL,
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL     Vercel system variables (run mode, preview
#                                     and callback origins, hosting disclosure)
#   VITEST                            set by Vitest; skips writes that only make
#                                     sense in a running server
